{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.83.1.a001", "note": "Vocative takes supplied *O* (rule 36).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.1.001"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.1.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001", "t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "PSA.83.1.a002", "note": "Prohibitive אַל → *not*.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.1.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.1.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "PSA.83.1.a003", "note": "Noun *silence*; the light verb goes to the possessive lamed, see next unit.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.1.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.1.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "PSA.83.1.a004", "note": "Verbless possessive clause ('let no silence be to thee'); the ASV's *keep* is the verb written for the possessive לְ predication (rules 43/49). Competing reading: *keep silence* as one light-verb unit on the noun with לְ unrepresented, or *keep* `added` under rule 20.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.1.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.1.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "PSA.83.1.a005", "note": "Suffix realized as subject pronoun *thou* (rule 40).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.1.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.1.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "PSA.83.1.a006", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.1.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.1.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "PSA.83.1.a007", "note": "Light verb *Hold ... peace* heads on the complement (rule 44); the *thy* of the fixed idiom is read as part of the verb's one rendering (rule 30). Competing reading: *thy* `added` under rule 18's closing sentence.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.1.007"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.1.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007", "t009", "t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "PSA.83.1.a008", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.1.008"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.1.008", "status": "