{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.83.16.a001", "note": "The bare second object 'shame' is reached through *with*, which the English verb's valency requires; it joins the verb (rule 44), discontinuous around the object.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.16.001"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.16.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001", "t004"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "PSA.83.16.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.16.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.16.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t003"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "PSA.83.16.a003", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.16.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.16.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "PSA.83.16.a004", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.16.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.16.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "PSA.83.16.a005", "note": "Waw rendered as purpose *That* (rule 14).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.16.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.16.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "PSA.83.16.a006", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.16.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.16.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007", "t008", "t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "PSA.83.16.a007", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.16.007"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.16.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "PSA.83.16.a008", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.16.008"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.16.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "PSA.83.16.a009", "note": "Vocative takes *O* (rule 36).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.16.009"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.16.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012", "t013"], "target_head": "t013"}], "ref": "PSA.83.16", "review_notes": [], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.83.17.a001", "note": "Jussive frame *Let them be* and the light-verb *put to shame* belong to the verb; head on *shame* (rules 17, 44).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.17.001"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.17.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001", "t002", "t003", "t004", "t005", "t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "PSA.83.17.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.17.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.17.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "PSA.83.17.a003", "note": "Shares the gapped *Let them be* frame of the first verb; takes only its own lexical word.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.17.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.17.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "PSA.83.17.a004", "note": "Construct עֲדֵי ('unto') rendered by the extent preposition *for*, exactly as rule 26 gives *for* to the עַד of וְעַד־עוֹלָם → *and for evermore*; split from *ever* under rule 2 because each morpheme has an English word of its own. Competing reading fuses *for ever* on the pair under rule 30, headed on עַד/ever; the accepted fusion was internally inconsistent (source head on the construct, target head on the word realizing the absolute).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.17.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.17.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "PSA.83.17.a005", "note": "Absolute עַד 'perpetuity' → *ever*.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.17.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.17.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "PSA.83.17.a006", "note": "Waw rendered *Yea* (rule 14).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.17.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.17.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "PSA.83.17.a007", "note": "Jussive frame belongs to the verb (rule 17).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.17.007"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.17.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012", "t013", "t014", "t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "PSA.83.17.a008", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.17.008"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.17.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "PSA.83.17.a009", "note": "Shares the gapped *let them be* frame.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.17.009"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.17.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t017"], "target_head": "t017"}], "ref": "PSA.83.17", "review_notes": ["Corrected עֲדֵי־עַד: the accepted unit fused *for ever* with source head on the construct עֲדֵי but target head on *ever*, which realizes the absolute עַד; each morpheme has a word of its own (*for* for the extent construct, *ever* for 'perpetuity'), so rule 2 splits them on the model of rule 26's *and for evermore*. Fused reading with head on עַד/*ever* named as the competing one."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.83.18.a001", "note": "Waw rendered as purpose *That* (rule 14).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.18.001"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.18.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "PSA.83.18.a002", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.18.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.18.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002", "t003", "t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "PSA.83.18.a003", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.18.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.18.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "PSA.83.18.a004", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.18.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.18.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t006"], "target_head": "t006"}, {"id": "PSA.83.18.a005", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.18.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.18.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "PSA.83.18.a006", "note": "Relative *whose* realizes the possessive suffix (rule 18).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.18.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.18.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "PSA.83.18.a007", "note": "Copula joins the predicate name (rule 20).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.18.007"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.18.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010", "t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "PSA.83.18.a008", "note": "לְבַד → *alone*, fused on the construct noun (rule 30). Margin reading set aside (rule 38).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.18.008", "WLC.PSA.83.18.009"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.18.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "PSA.83.18.a009", "note": "Suffix of לְבַדֶּךָ; the ASV writes no pronoun for it, *thou* being אַתָּה's (rule 40). Competing reading fuses it into *alone*.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.18.010"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.18.010", "status": "unrepresented", "target": [], "target_head": null}, {"id": "PSA.83.18.a010", "note": "Predicate adjective takes the copula *Art* and the supplied *the* (rules 20, 15); head on *High*.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.18.011"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.18.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012", "t013", "t014", "t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "PSA.83.18.a011", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.18.012"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.18.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t016"], "target_head": "t016"}, {"id": "PSA.83.18.a012", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.18.013"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.18.013", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t017"], "target_head": "t017"}, {"id": "PSA.83.18.a013", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.18.014"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.18.014", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t018"], "target_head": "t018"}, {"id": "PSA.83.18.a014", "note": "", "source": ["WLC.PSA.83.18.015"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.83.18.015", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t019"], "target_head": "t019"}], "ref": "PSA.83.18", "review_notes": ["ASV margin offers an alternative construal of *alone*; the printed text is aligned."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
